    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A multi-condition puzzle becomes easy if you unlock train length first. Suppose train A moves at 72 km/hr and crosses an opposite train half its own length moving at 36 km/hr in 10 s.\n\nRelative speed = 108 km/hr = 30 m/s. In 10 s, combined length = 300 m.\nBut combined length = 1.5L, so A is 200 m.",
